# Target C - matched all-train gap strengthens the terminal FREE package

**Date:** 2026-09-18  
**Status:** proof-only refinement; theorem-state authority unchanged  
**Scope:** full-core Type-II terminal FREE survivor sequences with `pi D-q=o(D)`  
**New input:** scope-safe matched all-train gap `g=0.007707`  
**Refines:** the 2026-09-18 terminal train/face bridge, rhombus-deficit floor, and chamber-interface floor  
**Certificate:** `research/verify_target_c_free_terminal_matched_gap_refinement_2026_09_18.py`  
**LEVEL I STATUS:** `STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.`

The terminal FREE chain written earlier today used the audited-working all-defect gap

\[
{2f-k\over D}\ge
\gamma-o(1),
\qquad
\gamma:=2s_2-\frac\pi2,
\qquad
s_2:=\sqrt{\frac\pi{2\sqrt3}}.
\]

The current research stack has a stronger scope-safe matched all-train theorem:

\[
\boxed{
\liminf {T-q/2\over D}\ge 2s_2+g,
\qquad g=0.007707.
}
\tag{MG.1}
\]

On the terminal face this improves the all-defect gap by exactly `g`. Propagating that
small atomic gain through the exact terminal ledgers improves all three current FREE
outputs simultaneously.

The strengthened constants are:

\[
\boxed{
 t_D+{2\over5}{Z_{ext}\over D}
 \ge
 2.153262849540479\ldots-o(1),
}
\tag{MG.2}
\]

\[
\boxed{
 \Delta_2D^2-R_4
 \ge
 (1.247399568236749\ldots-o(1))D
 +{4\over5}Z_{ext},
}
\tag{MG.3}
\]

\[
\boxed{
 (\Delta_2D^2-R_4)+{4\over5}(b-\operatorname{per}F)
 \ge
 (1.647399568236749\ldots-o(1))D,
}
\tag{MG.4}
\]

and, for the canonical raw inactive-chamber interface

\[
\mathcal H_D:=(b-\operatorname{per}F)+(Q+2f),
\]

\[
\boxed{
\liminf {\mathcal H_D\over D}
\ge2.294799136473498\ldots .
}
\tag{MG.5}
\]

Hence

\[
\boxed{
\liminf {A_{ch}-a_0Z_{ch}\over D}
\ge0.993677174384321\ldots,
\qquad a_0={\sqrt3\over2}.
}
\tag{MG.6}
\]

The classwise terminal split also strengthens to

\[
\boxed{
\max\{Q+2f,\ b-\operatorname{per}F\}
\ge(1.434249460295936\ldots-o(1))D,
}
\tag{MG.7}
\]

so one chamber class alone has Oler-weighted surplus at least

\[
\boxed{
(0.621048233990201\ldots-o(1))D.
}
\tag{MG.8}
\]

No claim in this note is canonicalized. The matched `g=0.007707` theorem itself is
proof-only, although its scope has already been hostile-audited and is used by other
current high-`t` notes.

---

## 1. Terminal conversion of the matched all-train theorem

Use the exact stopped-train identity

\[
T-q=2f-k.
\tag{MG.9}
\]

Then

\[
{T-q/2\over D}
={2f-k\over D}+{q\over2D}.
\]

Terminality gives `q/D->pi`, so (MG.1) implies

\[
\boxed{
{2f-k\over D}
\ge \gamma_g-o(1),
\qquad
\gamma_g:=\gamma+g.
}
\tag{MG.10}
\]

Numerically,

\[
\gamma_g=0.341536286933018\ldots .
\tag{MG.11}
\]

This is the only new input. Everything below is an exact re-propagation through the
already established terminal ledgers.

---

## 2. Strengthened FREE train/face bridge

The finite FREE-to-train/face bridge is unchanged:

\[
2t_D+z_D
\ge\pi+\phi_D+{1\over2}-o(1),
\tag{MG.12}
\]

where

\[
t_D={q-k\over D},
\qquad
z_D={Z_{ext}\over D},
\qquad
\phi_D={Q\over D}.
\]

Since `Q>=f`, (MG.10) and terminality imply

\[
\phi_D
\ge{\pi-t_D+\gamma_g\over2}-o(1).
\tag{MG.13}
\]

Substitution into (MG.12) gives

\[
5t_D+2z_D
\ge3\pi+1+\gamma_g-o(1).
\tag{MG.14}
\]

Therefore

\[
\boxed{
 t_D+{2\over5}z_D
 \ge C_{FREE,g}-o(1),
}
\tag{MG.15}
\]

with

\[
\begin{aligned}
C_{FREE,g}
&={\pi\over2}+{1\over5}+{2s_2\over5}+{g\over5}\\
&=2.153262849540479\ldots .
\end{aligned}
\tag{MG.16}
\]

Thus the previous constant `2.151721449540479...` increases by exactly

\[
{g\over5}=0.0015414.
\]

The exterior-population price becomes

\[
\boxed{
 z_D\ge {3\pi+1+\gamma_g-5t_D\over2}-o(1).
}
\tag{MG.17}
\]

For reference,

\[
\begin{array}{c|c}
T & t_D\le T\ \Longrightarrow\ \liminf Z_{ext}/D\\ \hline
1.8440 & 0.773157123851198\ldots\\
1.8600 & 0.733157123851198\ldots\\
1.8687 & 0.711407123851198\ldots\\
2.0000 & 0.383157123851198\ldots
\end{array}
\tag{MG.18}
\]

At `z_D=o(1)` the new floor is

\[
\boxed{
\liminf t_D\ge2.153262849540479\ldots .
}
\tag{MG.19}
\]

At the relaxed scalar endpoint, `lambda_D=(b-per(F))` still satisfies

\[
{\lambda_D\over D}={1\over2},
\]

while

\[
{f\over D}={Q\over D}
=0.664933045491166\ldots .
\]

---

## 3. Strengthened rhombus-count deficit

Let

\[
\mathcal D_4:=\Delta_2D^2-R_4,
\qquad
\Delta_2={\pi\over2\sqrt3}.
\]

The exact full-source Oler bridge remains

\[
\mathcal D_4
\ge(q-k)+f+Z_{ch}+Z_{ext}-{\pi\over2}D.
\tag{MG.20}
\]

Drop `Z_ch`, use (MG.10), and normalize:

\[
{\mathcal D_4\over D}
\ge {t_D\over2}+z_D+{\gamma_g\over2}-o(1).
\tag{MG.21}
\]

Rewrite the right side as

\[
{1\over2}\left(t_D+{2\over5}z_D\right)
+{4\over5}z_D+{\gamma_g\over2}.
\]

Using (MG.15),

\[
\boxed{
{\mathcal D_4\over D}
\ge B_g+{4\over5}z_D-o(1),
}
\tag{MG.22}
\]

where

\[
\begin{aligned}
B_g
&={C_{FREE,g}+\gamma_g\over2}\\
&={1\over10}+{6s_2\over5}+{3g\over5}\\
&=1.247399568236749\ldots .
\end{aligned}
\tag{MG.23}
\]

This proves (MG.3). The previous baseline `1.242775368236749...` increases by
`3g/5=0.0046242`.

The terminal FREE metric recipient law

\[
\lambda_D+Z_{ext}\ge{D\over2}-o(D)
\tag{MG.24}
\]

then gives

\[
\boxed{
\mathcal D_4+{4\over5}\lambda_D
\ge(W_g-o(1))D,
}
\tag{MG.25}
\]

where

\[
W_g=B_g+{2\over5}
=1.647399568236749\ldots .
\tag{MG.26}
\]

Consequently

\[
\boxed{
\max\{\mathcal D_4,\lambda_D\}
\ge(0.915221982353749\ldots-o(1))D.
}
\tag{MG.27}
\]

Indeed, if both were below `xD`, then the left side of (MG.25) would be below
`(9/5)xD`.

The geometric form of (MG.22), using

\[
a_0\mathcal D_4=\delta_F+A_{ch}+E_4,
\]

is

\[
\boxed{
\delta_F+A_{ch}+E_4
\ge(1.080279714762765\ldots-o(1))D
+{2\sqrt3\over5}Z_{ext}.
}
\tag{MG.28}
\]

The weighted version is

\[
\boxed{
\delta_F+A_{ch}+E_4
+{2\sqrt3\over5}\lambda_D
\ge(1.426689876276540\ldots-o(1))D.
}
\tag{MG.29}
\]

Inside the old high-`t` window the stronger exterior price and stronger baseline add
exactly `g` to the old rhombus-deficit table. For example,

\[
t_D\le1.8687
\Longrightarrow
{\mathcal D_4\over D}
\ge1.816525267317708\ldots-o(1).
\tag{MG.30}
\]

---

## 4. Strengthened terminal chamber-interface floor

The exact terminal identities are

\[
Q+\lambda_D=2(q-k)-\operatorname{per}(F),
\tag{MG.31}
\]

and, because `q<=per(F)<=pi D` on the terminal face,

\[
{\operatorname{per}(F)\over D}\to\pi.
\tag{MG.32}
\]

Equation (MG.10) gives

\[
{f\over D}
\ge{\pi-t_D+\gamma_g\over2}-o(1).
\tag{MG.33}
\]

Since `Q>=f` and `lambda_D>=0`, (MG.31) implies

\[
2t_D-\pi\ge {f\over D}-o(1).
\tag{MG.34}
\]

Combining (MG.33)--(MG.34) yields the terminal feasibility floor

\[
\boxed{
 t_D\ge t_{0,g}-o(1),
\qquad
 t_{0,g}:={3\pi+\gamma_g\over5}
 ={\pi\over2}+{2s_2\over5}+{g\over5}
 =1.953262849540479\ldots .
}
\tag{MG.35}
\]

For

\[
\mathcal H_D:=\lambda_D+Q+2f
=2(q-k)-\operatorname{per}(F)+2f,
\]

(MG.33) gives

\[
{\mathcal H_D\over D}
\ge t_D+\gamma_g-o(1).
\]

Thus

\[
\boxed{
\liminf {\mathcal H_D\over D}
\ge t_{0,g}+\gamma_g
={12s_2\over5}+{6g\over5}
=2.294799136473498\ldots .
}
\tag{MG.36}
\]

Canonical Section 85 then gives

\[
\boxed{
\liminf {A_{ch}-a_0Z_{ch}\over D}
\ge {\sqrt3\over4}
\left({12s_2\over5}+{6g\over5}\right)
=0.993677174384321\ldots .
}
\tag{MG.37}
\]

The relaxed scalar system for this total interface floor is sharp at

\[
 t=t_{0,g},\qquad
 {f\over D}={Q\over D}
 ={4s_2+2g\over5},
\qquad
 {\lambda_D\over D}=0.
\tag{MG.38}
\]

---

## 5. Strengthened classwise split

Normalize `F=f/D`, `Qbar=Q/D`, and `L=lambda_D/D`. The raw exceptional and outer
interface classes are

\[
E:=2F+Qbar,
\qquad L.
\]

Since `Qbar>=F`,

\[
E\ge3F.
\tag{MG.39}
\]

From (MG.33),

\[
t_D\ge\pi+\gamma_g-2F-o(1).
\]

Using

\[
E+L={\mathcal H_D\over D}
=2t_D-\pi+2F+o(1),
\]

we get

\[
E+L\ge4s_2+2g-2F-o(1).
\]

Therefore

\[
\max\{E,L\}
\ge
\max\{3F,\ 2s_2+g-F\}-o(1).
\tag{MG.40}
\]

The right side is minimized at

\[
F={2s_2+g\over4},
\]

with value

\[
\boxed{
{3(2s_2+g)\over4}
={3s_2\over2}+{3g\over4}
=1.434249460295936\ldots .
}
\tag{MG.41}
\]

This proves (MG.7). The separate Section-67 Oler inequalities

\[
A_{exc}-a_0Z_{def}\ge c_0(Q+2f),
\qquad
H_{out}-a_0Z_{in}\ge c_0\lambda_D
\]

then give (MG.8):

\[
\boxed{
\max\{A_{exc}-a_0Z_{def},\ H_{out}-a_0Z_{in}\}
\ge(0.621048233990201\ldots-o(1))D.
}
\tag{MG.42}
\]

The classwise scalar relaxation is sharp at

\[
{f\over D}={Q\over D}={2s_2+g\over4},
\quad
 t={\pi\over2}+s_2+{g\over2},
\quad
 {\lambda_D\over D}={3(2s_2+g)\over4}.
\tag{MG.43}
\]

---

## 6. What changed and what did not

This refinement adds one proof-only input and changes no exact finite identity.
Relative to the three earlier terminal notes, the safe improvements are:

\[
\begin{array}{c|c|c}
\text{quantity} & \text{previous} & \text{matched-gap refinement}\\ \hline
 t+(2/5)z & 2.151721449540479 & 2.153262849540479\\
 \mathcal D_4/D\text{ baseline} & 1.242775368236749 & 1.247399568236749\\
 (\mathcal D_4+0.8\lambda)/D & 1.642775368236749 & 1.647399568236749\\
 \mathcal H_D/D & 2.285550736473497 & 2.294799136473498\\
 (A_{ch}-a_0Z_{ch})/D & 0.989672499712141 & 0.993677174384321\\
 \max(Q+2f,\lambda)/D & 1.428469210295936 & 1.434249460295936
\end{array}
\tag{MG.44}
\]

The authoritative theorem-state ledger is unchanged. The `g=0.007707` theorem is
proof-only, so all improvements in this note remain proof-only as well.

The matched-gap architecture is already nearly numerically exhausted: its own exact
certificate has only a small positive margin at `g=0.007707`. More scalar optimization
inside this same package can therefore change the terminal constants only marginally.
The remaining work is geometric.

## 7. Remaining bottleneck

The terminal FREE survivor now has to pay all of the following simultaneously:

\[
\mathcal D_4
\ge(1.2473995682\ldots-o(1))D+0.8Z_{ext},
\]

\[
\mathcal H_D
\ge(2.2947991364\ldots-o(1))D,
\]

and

\[
\max\{Q+2f,\ b-\operatorname{per}F\}
\ge(1.4342494602\ldots-o(1))D.
\]

The next closing theorem must use the geometry of one of the two interface classes.
In the exceptional-face class, the target is a transfer from `Q+2f` and the
first-order rhombus deficit into the occurrence-counted Section-122/123 attachment-cell
detour. In the outer class, the target is a source-preserving diameter descent or an
upper budget for a `>=1.434D` actual outer-walk detour in the terminal near-disk hull.

**Disposition:** propagated the scope-safe matched all-train gap through the complete
terminal FREE scalar package. C-II remains open.
